<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-8 py-16">
<h2 class="font-headline text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-8 tracking-tighter">What the quote covers</h2>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-tertiary text-3xl mb-4">water_drop</span>
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold text-on-surface mb-2">Draining</h3>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">We can handle the drain on site. If you've already drained it, the job is cheaper and goes faster.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-tertiary text-3xl mb-4">power</span>
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold text-on-surface mb-2">Electrical disconnect</h3>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">We disconnect the whip at the tub side once you confirm the breaker is off. We don't pull the subpanel side; that's an electrician's job.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-tertiary text-3xl mb-4">construction</span>
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold text-on-surface mb-2">Disassembly</h3>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">Most tubs won't fit through a side gate whole. We cut with a reciprocating saw, bundle the pieces, keep the foam mess contained.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-tertiary text-3xl mb-4">fence</span>
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold text-on-surface mb-2">Fence panel access</h3>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">If we need to pull fence panels to get the tub out, we do. We put them back when the job is done.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-tertiary text-3xl mb-4">local_shipping</span>
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold text-on-surface mb-2">Hauling</h3>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">Shell to the dump. Motor, pump, and copper plumbing to scrap metal. Everything metal gets recycled, not landfilled.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-tertiary text-3xl mb-4">cleaning_services</span>
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold text-on-surface mb-2">Cleanup</h3>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">The pad or deck where the tub sat should look like the tub was never there. No foam shreds, no splinters.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- What makes the price move -->
<section class="bg-surface-container-low py-20 px-8">
<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
<h2 class="font-headline text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-8 tracking-tighter">What moves the price</h2>
<div class="space-y-4">
<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold pr-4">Access and path out</h3><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span></summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant">The biggest variable. A 4-foot side gate straight to the driveway is cheap. A built-in deck with a narrow 30-inch gate means more disassembly and longer loading time.</div>
</details>
<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold pr-4">Size</h3><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span></summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant">Anything bigger than a standard 7x7 footprint, or swim-spa hybrids, run at the higher end of the range.</div>
</details>
<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold pr-4">Cover, surround, or gazebo</h3><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span></summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant">A vinyl cover is free. A built-in cedar surround or a gazebo adds demolition time ($150 to $400 depending on scope).</div>
</details>
<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold pr-4">Drained &amp; disconnected before we arrive</h3><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span></summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant">Drained tubs, with the breaker off for 24 hours, save 1 to 2 hours of on-site time. That's reflected in the lower end of the range.</div>
</details>
<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none"><h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold pr-4">Same-day or rush</h3><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span></summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant">Possible when the tub is already drained and the breaker is off. Rush jobs carry a percentage premium, quoted on the first text.</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>
</section>

